      description: "Acoramidis is an oral transthyretin thyroxine-pocket binder and kinetic stabilizer for wild-type or variant ATTR cardiomyopathy. Because tetramer dissociation is the rate-limiting first committed step in ATTR amyloid formation, keeping TTR tetramers assembled reduces the supply of monomers that can misfold into toxic oligomers and fibrils. The 712-mg twice-daily regimen produced near-complete in-vitro TTR stabilization by Day 28 in the labeled pharmacodynamic assay; that finding confirms target engagement, but it does not mean established myocardial amyloid has disappeared or that congestion will improve immediately.",
