      nursingEssentials: ["Before infusion assess suicidality, bipolar/psychosis symptoms, CNS depressants, respiratory disease, falls, IV access, caregiver/child-safety plan and end-stage renal disease, in which the solubilizing excipient can accumulate.", "Maintain continuous observation and pulse oximetry; distinguish sleep from unresponsiveness, protect airway and infant, stop rather than merely slow for hypoxia or loss of consciousness, and reassess before resumption."],
