      contraindications: ["Contraindicated with strong CYP3A4 inhibitors because greatly increased ubrogepant exposure can increase adverse effects.", "Contraindicated after serious hypersensitivity to ubrogepant or an excipient. Avoid end-stage renal disease; dose adjustment is required in severe renal or hepatic impairment."],
      interactions: ["Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors are contraindicated; moderate or weak inhibitors require a lower regimen. Strong CYP3A inducers should be avoided because reduced exposure is expected to cause loss of efficacy.", "P-gp or BCRP-only inhibitors can raise exposure and may require dose modification. Ask specifically about antimicrobials, anticonvulsants, transplant drugs, and supplements rather than relying on the patient to recognize enzyme names."],
      nursingEssentials: ["Verify attack onset, 50- or 100-mg dose, whether a second dose is permitted at least 2 hours later, 200-mg daily maximum, interacting CYP3A/P-gp/BCRP drugs, renal/hepatic adjustment and pregnancy context.", "Assess headache red flags and medication-overuse pattern; monitor nausea, somnolence, blood pressure, painful pale/blue digits and delayed hypersensitivity."],
